      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-313290",
      ":question/problem": "A fitness company reported that the average daily step count for a random sample of its users was $11, 200$ steps, with an associated margin of error of $450$ steps. The study was then repeated with a much larger sample size, and the new sample\u2019s mean and margin of error were calculated in the same way as in the original study.\n\nWhich of the following statements is most likely true?\n\n1. The margin of error from the new study is smaller than the margin of error from the original study.\n2. The mean from the new study is larger than the mean from the original study.\n3. The mean from the new study is $11, 200$ steps."
    },
