      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-313292",
      ":question/problem": "A nutritionist reported that the average sugar content of a random sample of protein bars was $19.6g$, with a margin of error of $1.2g$. The study was then repeated with a much smaller sample size, and the new sample\u2019s mean and margin of error were calculated in the same way as in the original study.\n\nWhich of the following statements is most likely true?\n\n1. The margin of error from the new study is less than $1.2g$.\n2. The margin of error from the new study is larger than the margin of error from the original study.\n3. The mean of the new study is larger than the mean of the original study."
    }
